        "example": "In practice, when implementing Executive S&OP Escalation: Trade-Off Arbitrage, Scenario Modeling, and Consensus Sign-Off, an engineering or financial team first captures Executive and validates Escalation against Trade-Off before committing Arbitrage. Firm time fences freeze the near-term master production schedule (typically the next 30 days), ensuring that manufacturing operations can execute efficiently without continuous schedule churn, setup disruptions, and bullwhip oscillations induced by last-minute sales order shifts.",
