          "why": "An Original Negotiable Maritime Bill of Lading is a formal Document of Title. Unlike an Air Waybill (which is merely a transport receipt and contract of carriage), whoever holds the properly endorsed original Bill of Lading legally owns the cargo, preventing the carrier from releasing goods without physical surrender of the original document."
