        "example": "In practice, when implementing Hazmat Segregation Matrix & Cold Chain Telemetry Engine: Automated Hazard Verification and Thermal Excursion Auditing, an engineering or financial team first captures Hazmat and validates Segregation against Matrix before committing Chain. An automated stop-shipment interlock ensures system-enforced compliance: the instant an incompatible chemical combination is detected on a shipment manifest, the software prevents warehouse pick, pack, and container loading operations, making it physically and legally impossible to co-load hazardous materials that violate international segregation laws.",
        "code": "# Hazmat Segregation Matrix & Cold Chain Telemetry Engine: Automated Hazard Verification and Thermal Excursion Auditing — Quantitative Verification Model (Day 54, Part 5)\ndef evaluate_hazmat(hazmat_base: float, segregation_rate_pct: float) -> dict:\n    adjustment = round(hazmat_base * (segregation_rate_pct / 100.0), 2)\n    net_position = round(hazmat_base - adjustment, 2)\n    coverage_ratio = round(net_position / max(adjustment, 1.0), 2)\n    return {\n        \"module\": \"Hazmat Segregation Matrix & Cold Chain Telemetry\",\n        \"hazmat_base\": hazmat_base,\n        \"segregation_adjustment\": adjustment,\n        \"net_verified_position\": net_position,\n        \"coverage_ratio\": coverage_ratio,\n    }\n\nreport = evaluate_hazmat(238750.0, 31.0)\nprint(f\"[{report['module']}] Base: {report['hazmat_base']:,.2f} | Adj (31%): {report['segregation_adjustment']:,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Net Position: {report['net_verified_position']:,.2f} | Coverage Ratio: {report['coverage_ratio']}x | Status: VERIFIED\")",
