      "Part 2 (State-Space Modeling, Queueing Networks & SimEvents / AnyLogic Architectures): A machine enters a 'Blocked' state (specifically Blocking-After-Service) when it finishes processing a part but is physically prevented from releasing it because the downstream buffer or workstation has reached maximum capacity.",
